{
  "_readme": [
    "Shared behavioural fixture for the workspace-mutation guard: every case",
    "is executed by BOTH `.claude/hooks/guard_workspace_mutation.py` and the",
    "TypeScript mirror in `cline-plugins/cline-agents/index.ts`, so the two",
    "implementations are pinned to the same OUTCOMES rather than merely to",
    "the same structure (deagy/cadre#222). Driven by",
    "`plugin/tools/test_guard_parity.py`; the TypeScript half runs through",
    "`plugin/tools/guard_parity_runner.mjs` and is SKIPPED, not failed, when",
    "node or a TypeScript transform is unavailable.",
    "",
    "A case declares `setup` (steps replayed into a disposable repository),",
    "`command`, optional `cwd`, and the `expected` decision. `blocked` cases",
    "may also assert `reason_contains`, which is what makes the string-",
    "handling divergences #222 names (a truncating `split`, `??` where the",
    "other file means `or`) observable at all -- both guards agreeing on",
    "'blocked' would hide a ref that one of them silently cut short.",
    "",
    "Placeholders: {repo}, {tmp}, {wt:<name>} (a worktree's registered path).",
    "Setup ops: commit, dirty, untracked, branch, branch-at, worktree,",
    "detach-worktree, age-worktree, mkdir, config-alias.",
    "`wrap_in_bash_c: N` wraps the command in N layers of `bash -c '...'`,",
    "quoted once in the harness so both guards are handed the same string."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "reset-hard-dirty-blocked",
      "issue": "129",
      "why": "Baseline: the original incident shape must stay blocked in both guards.",
      "setup": [
        {
          "op": "commit",
          "path": "a.txt",
          "content": "one"
        },
        {
          "op": "dirty",
          "path": "a.txt",
          "content": "uncommitted"
        }
      ],
      "command": "git reset --hard",
      "expected": "blocked",
      "reason_contains": "uncommitted changes"
    },
