      "issue": "222",
      "why": "Found by code review. A bare `-` ends option processing like `--`, so the following `-c` is an operand: `bash - -c \"...\"` makes bash treat `-c` as a script FILENAME and fail with 'No such file or directory' -- the git command never runs. Verified by execution. Python returned None here; the TypeScript loop fell through `-` and returned the script, blocking a command that does nothing. A real divergence, in the over-blocking direction.",
